# Minimum mutation kill rate (%), enforced by scripts/mutation_score.py in
# the mutation job of reusable-python-ci.yml.
#
# Measured at 66.67% (4 killed of 6 testable). The two survivors are
# equivalent mutants in clamp: `value < low` becoming `value <= low`
# returns `low` when the two are equal, which is the answer the original
# gives, so no test can tell them apart. A fixture that pretends every
# mutant is killable would misrepresent what real repos see.
#
# 65 sits just under the measured rate, which is how a real repo should
# set this: from a complete run, not from an aspiration. Ratchet it up as
# the suite improves. Lowering it requires a justification in the pull
# request that does so. First non-comment, non-blank line wins.
65
